<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>💨 LIVE WIND — NORTH AMERICA</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wind_na/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Wind (MODEL analysis): speed m/s &rarr; kt (x1.94384) &rarr; WMO Beaufort 0-12. Arrows point TOWARD motion. Calm (&lt;0.5 m/s) draws no arrow.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP GLWU v2.1 surface U/V (Great Lakes water) + HRRR 3km 10m U/V + RRFS North American 10m U/V + ECCC GDPS fallback).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>💨 LIVE WIND — NORTH AMERICA — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/North_America_Live_Wind.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>900</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
